  "name": "Jackson §12.4: gradient drift",
  "description": "Jackson §12.4 (particle drifts in nonuniform, static magnetic fields). A row of magnets makes the field stronger towards the bottom. A gyrating ion's orbit is tighter where the field is stronger, so it drifts sideways, along the lines of equal |B|: the positive ion to the left, the negative one to the right. Bring each into its detector. A charge adds an E×B drift that is the same for both signs; a magnet changes the gradient, which moves them in opposite directions.",
